BUILDS 89 + 90 - Travel NPCs answer again, and Dagon wakes up

BUILD 89 - the Warden of the Spartan Crypt (and every travel NPC) responds again
- FIXED: the Warden of the Spartan Crypt did nothing when clicked. No dialog box, no
  travel option. He now opens his menu and takes you down into the crypt, which is the
  canonical way into that area.
- The same defect affected every traveller you reach by teleporting in: the
  return-to-Helos NPCs in the Soulvizier areas and the enter-offer travellers. All 30
  travel NPCs are fixed by the same change.
- Cause: an NPC you arrive at by teleport was never woken up, so the game drew him but
  he had no clickable state. Every travel NPC is now woken before his travel offer is
  presented, using the same method the working Leinth exit portal has always used.
- The Helos plaza travellers that already worked keep the exact same routes and
  destinations. No route, destination or dialog option changed anywhere.

BUILD 90 - Dagon, Lord of the Poisoned Deep no longer stands frozen
- FIXED: Dagon stood frozen in place. He now walks, runs, attacks, staggers, dies and
  casts Tidal Strike, his signature move, for the first time.
- The bug dates back to the original Soulvizier: Dagon was built out of the Hydra, and
  every animation clip pointed at the 101-bone Hydra skeleton while his actual body is
  a 30-bone deep-one mage. He is now bound to his own rig, the one the base game uses
  for his same-body relatives.
- NEW PERMANENT GATE: no monster can ship any more with animations that cannot drive
  its body (the same freeze class that once took the maenad thrown-weapon fighters).
- Nothing else about Dagon changed: same fight, same skills, same soul, same drop
  chance, same orb.

Quest data plus database. No map or text change beyond these fixes: your characters,
saves and items are untouched. Fully quit the game and restart Steam to pick up the
update.
